  ],
  "inline_comments": [
    {
      "body": "![critical](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/critical.svg)\n\nThe `pip install -e \".[trtllm]\"` command requires the project's source code to be present in the Docker image, as it looks for a `setup.py` or `pyproject.toml` file in the current working directory. It appears the `COPY` instruction to add the source code is missing. Without it, the Docker build will fail.\n\nTo fix this, you should copy the project source into the image before attempting to install it.\n\n```\nCOPY . .\nRUN pip install -e \".[trtllm]\"\n```",
      "created_at": "2026-03-20T23:19:35Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -50,3 +50,5 @@ RUN pip uninstall -y verl\n # ==============================================================================\n # Note: The NGC image already includes a pre-installed TensorRT-LLM, but you can install a specific version if needed.\n # Refer to https://nvidia.github.io/TensorRT-LLM/installation/index.html for more details.\n+\n+RUN pip install -e \".[trtllm]\"",
